@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Reference / design method. Native Git/OO/data notation illustration, not a commitment to advanced product features.
title Proposed publication use-case classes — selected technical illustration
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam classBorderColor #64748B
top to bottom direction
class PublishRevisionHandler {
 +handle(command : PublishIntent) : PublicationOutcome
}
class PublishIntent {
 +actorId : ActorId
 +resumeId : ResumeId
 +expectedDraftVersion : RevisionId
 +commandId : CommandId
}
class ResumeDraft {
 -version : RevisionId
 -selectedContent : ConfirmedSelection
 +snapshot(expected : RevisionId) : DraftSnapshot
}
class PublishedResumeRevision <<immutable>> {
 +revisionId : RevisionId
 +sourceDraftVersion : RevisionId
 +artifactManifest : ManifestReference
}
interface PublicationStore {
 +commitConfirmedRevision(intent, snapshot) : PublicationOutcome
}
interface ResourceAuthority {
 +requirePublish(actorId, resumeId) : AuthorizedContext
}
class PersistenceAdapter <<infrastructure>>
PublishRevisionHandler --> PublishIntent : validates
PublishRevisionHandler --> ResourceAuthority : current operation scope
PublishRevisionHandler --> ResumeDraft : confirmed version only
PublishRevisionHandler --> PublicationStore : bounded atomic persistence contract
PublicationStore ..> PublishedResumeRevision : records identity and live pointer
PersistenceAdapter ..|> PublicationStore
ResourceAuthority -[hidden]down-> ResumeDraft
ResumeDraft -[hidden]down-> PublishIntent
PublishIntent -[hidden]down-> PublicationStore
note bottom of PublishedResumeRevision
 Actual submission materials remain independent.
 No automatic profile-edit publication.
 Exact types/signatures are proposed, not implemented.
end note
@enduml
